{"attribution":{"text":"Wikipedia (CC BY-SA 4.0)","photos":"Wikimedia Commons, see each photo","thumbs":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/","width":500},"marinas":{"1132":{"n":"Κατάκολο","p":[["c/cc/Katakolo_dock_2010.jpg","Katakolo dock 2010","Wknight94 talk","CC BY-SA 3.0",0.67],["6/69/Katakolo_smoke_2010.jpg","Katakolo smoke 2010","Wknight94 talk","CC BY-SA 3.0",0.67],["2/2e/Star_Princess-2011.jpg","Star Princess-2011","Mazepa11","CC BY-SA 3.0",0.6],["9/9f/Katakolon_-_panoramio.jpg","Katakolon","patano","CC BY-SA 3.0",0.67],["e/e3/Katakolon_-_panoramio_-_patano.jpg","Katakolon","patano","CC BY-SA 3.0",0.67],["8/84/Travels_in_Greece_-_panoramio.jpg","Travels in Greece","Basilis petroulakis","CC BY-SA 3.0",0.75]],"a":["Katakolo","Katakolo (Greek: Κατάκολο) is a seaside village in the municipality of Pyrgos in western Elis, Greece. It is situated on a headland overlooking the Ionian Sea and separating the Gulf of Kyparissia from the rest of the Ionian. It is 11 km (6.8 mi) west of Pyrgos. The small village of Agios Andreas, which in ancient times was the natural harbour for Ancient Olympia, lies northwest of Katakolo."]},"1225":{"n":"A.N.O.Z","p":[["7/73/Jewish_cemetery_Zakynthos_01.jpg","Jewish cemetery Zakynthos 01","Nikodem Nijaki","CC BY-SA 3.0",0.83],["6/62/English_cemetery_Zakynthos_01.jpg","English cemetery Zakynthos 01","Nikodem Nijaki","CC BY-SA 3.0",0.78],["1/1b/Bochali_291_00%2C_Greece_-_panoramio.jpg","Bochali 291 00, Greece","Andreas Alexandris","CC BY-SA 3.0",0.75]],"a":["St. Mark's Roman Catholic Church","Saint Mark's Roman Catholic Church (Greek: Ιερός Ναός Αγίου Μάρκου) is located on the St. Mark square in the city of Zakynthos, Greece, and holds the distinction of being the only Catholic church on the island with this name."]},"3381":{"n":"Λιμάνι","p":[["9/95/Kyparissia%2C_Greece_-_panoramio.jpg","Kyparissia, Greece","stathop","CC BY-SA 3.0",0.75],["9/9a/Kyparissia_-_panoramio.jpg","Kyparissia","stathop","CC BY-SA 3.0",0.75],["c